"""The prototype engine's values that EMR's tests compare against.

The prototype engine is the frozen engine release 0.1.0 shipped beside EMR. The tests of this
package do not run it: a test that compares EMR against it asks prototype_reference.prototype_value
for its side, which returns the value recorded here for the test's case and the sha256 of its
inputs. The research repository's recorder wrote this file: it ran the research tests that compare
EMR against the prototype engine live, on the CPU, and recorded only after every one of them had
passed. Values are exact (arrays by dtype, shape and zlib-compressed bytes in hex, floats by
float.hex) and kept per CPU architecture, with the research commit and the versions they were
recorded with, and "xla_flags", the XLA_FLAGS conditions they were recorded under (unset, and
--xla_cpu_multi_thread_eigen=false: on x86-64 some inputs EMR computes depend on it); "agree" says
whether the two architectures recorded the same values for the same inputs (None until both are
recorded). Do not edit by hand: record again.
"""

